            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0407" n="397" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg397"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10–2246</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-10-22T13:00:00+08:00">October 22, 1946—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 22—10:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1711. Minority party leaders, top Government representatives and others, having
                    persuaded Chou En-lai to return to capital from Shanghai with them, President
                    Chiang sent for me on morning of October 21, before leaving for Formosa, to
                    define his policy as follows:</p>
                <p>Having formally delivered his published communication of October 18 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">16</hi>] through General Marshall and me to the
                    Communist delegates, he indicated they should in like manner send a written
                    reply. If favorable, the discussions should follow the procedure and be confined
                    within the terms of his communication. Every encouragement should be given the
                    minority parties to take an active share in preparation for and joining in the
                    National Assembly.</p>
                <p>Generalissimo’s trip to Formosa had been long planned and his departure postponed
                    one day in order to see Chou and minority party leaders, its coming at this time
                    being purely a coincidence.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
